# Build context for backend/Dockerfile is the repo root (the backend is a pub
# workspace member and cannot resolve without `packages/shared`).
#
# Secrets first: `backend/.env` holds the real Postgres password, and
# `dart_frog build` copies it into its output directory. Neither may ever reach
# an image layer — the deployed app gets these from Fly secrets instead. This
# list also bounds what `fly deploy --remote-only` uploads to the builder.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Generated / resolved state. The image resolves its own.
**/.dart_tool/
**/.dart_frog/
backend/build/
frontend/build/
**/pubspec_overrides.yaml

# Not needed to compile the API.
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.agents/
.claude/
.serena/
brand/
frontend/
**/*.iml
README.md

# `tools/` is developer tooling, except for the one piece the backend resolves:
# `collector` is a workspace member and a dev dependency of `backend`, and
# `dart pub get` resolves dev dependencies too. Excluding it fails the build
# with "could not find package collector at https://pub.dev", which reads like
# a typo rather than a missing build context. Nothing from it reaches the final
# image — that stage is `FROM scratch` and copies only the compiled binary.
tools/
!tools/collector
!tools/collector/**

# The exception above is a blanket one, and the last matching pattern wins — so
# everything the blocks above already excluded has to be excluded again here,
# scoped, or it comes back in through `tools/collector/`. Keep this block last.
tools/collector/.env
tools/collector/.env.*
tools/collector/.dart_tool
tools/collector/.dart_tool/**
tools/collector/pubspec_overrides.yaml
